+**🔥 BOSS 1 + BOSS 3 FIXES — ANTI-STUCK ARCHITECTURE + ARITHMETIC (2026-08-22).**
+
+Founder: *"I have been trying to get the 1st boss and the final boss to be fixed
+for the longest time now."* Both bosses had the same root class of bug: the boss
+gets stuck against geometry and pogo-jumps in place forever, reading as "floating"
+or "not moving past this point." Six+ prior fix attempts across multiple AI models
+(Kimi K3, Grok 4.6, Qwen3, DeepSeek, Codex) all addressed symptoms, not the
+underlying architecture.
+
+**What was actually wrong (both bosses share the same root cause):**
+
+1. **Leap arithmetic deficit (Boss 1):** LEAP_VELOCITY -620 clears 196px at
+   gravity 980. Level 1 platforms need 200px (4px short) and 350px (1px short
+   with double jump). The boss could never reach platforms and pogo'd under them.
+   **Fix:** LEAP_VELOCITY -630 (202px), AIR_JUMP_VELOCITY -570 (368px total).
+   Same fix applied to Claim Jumper's HOP_VELOCITY/AIR_HOP_VELOCITY.
+
+2. **Wall-pogo loop (Boss 3):** The end wall at x=4400 uses World collision
+   layer (not player_only). The boss's body overlaps it even after
+   `_clamp_to_arena()` pulls his centre back. `is_on_wall()` returns true every
+   frame, triggering a hop. The hop's cooldown (0.7s) is shorter than airtime
+   (1.28s), so the boss never gets a grounded chase frame — he pogo's in place
+   against the wall forever. **Fix:** Arena-boundary guard suppresses
+   `is_on_wall()` hop when the boss is at an arena boundary. The clamp handles
+   containment; the wall-hop was pure harm.
+
+3. **No anti-stuck architecture (both bosses):** When stuck (no horizontal
+   progress for N seconds while the player is beyond reach), neither boss had a
+   general "try something different" behavior. Every prior fix was a per-prop
+   exception. **Fix:** Anti-stuck progress timer on both bosses. If no progress
+   for 2.0s while player is >120px away, force a vault: leap + horizontal commit
+   toward player at 1.3x patrol speed, with air-jump armed. 3s cooldown.
+
+4. **Horizontal commit on wall-leap (Boss 1):** Wall-leaps set velocity.y but
+   left velocity.x at whatever `move_and_slide()` produced — often ~0 against a
+   wall. The boss went straight up and came straight back down onto the same
+   wall. **Fix:** Wall-leaps now commit horizontal velocity toward the player.
+
+**Files changed:**
+- `src/boss/auditor.gd` — LEAP_VELOCITY, AIR_JUMP_VELOCITY, wall-leap commit,
+  anti-stuck vault
+- `src/boss/claim_jumper.gd` — HOP_VELOCITY, AIR_HOP_VELOCITY, arena-boundary
+  guard, anti-stuck vault
+
+**What this does NOT claim:** Playwright frames and live hard-refresh
+verification are still needed. The arithmetic and architecture are correct;
+only a real export + browser test proves the fix end-to-end. Run
+`node scripts/verify-game.mjs <url>` after deploying.
+
+**Multi-model workspace guide:** `docs/multi-model-guide.md` — how to set up
+CLAUDE.md + CONTEXT.md for multiple AI models working on the same repo.
+
+---
+
