+# Multi-Model Workspace Guide
+
+## The Problem
+
+You are using multiple AI models (Claude, Kimi K3, Grok 4.6, Qwen3, DeepSeek,
+Codex, etc.) on the same repo. Each model needs different context to do its job.
+Giving every model the full repo burns context windows. Giving each model its
+own competing CLAUDE.md creates drift.
+
+## The Solution: One CLAUDE.md, Focused Packets
+
+**You do NOT need separate CLAUDE.md files per model.** The root `CLAUDE.md` is
+the single entry point for ALL models. It contains:
+
+1. Project identity (what this game is)
+2. Workspace routing table (| Task | Go to | Read | Skills |)
+3. Non-negotiable rules (security, web export, wallet gate, naming)
+4. ALWAYS-SHIP rule (update STATUS.md, commit, push)
+
+Each model reads `CLAUDE.md` first, then follows the routing table to the
+relevant workspace's `CONTEXT.md`, which gives standards and patterns for that
+area.
+
+## How to Give Each Model Its Task
+
+Instead of separate CLAUDE.md files, give each model a **focused context
+packet** — a short prompt that says:
+
+1. What to fix (the specific bug or feature)
+2. Which files to read (exact paths from the routing table)
+3. Which shared model the change belongs in (the autoload/base class)
+4. What acceptance looks like (the gate that proves it works)
+5. What NOT to touch (the guardrails)
+
+### Example: Kimi K3 does jump math
+
+```
+TASK: Verify the Auditor's leap arithmetic against Level 1 platform heights.
+READ: src/boss/auditor.gd (LEAP_VELOCITY, AIR_JUMP_VELOCITY constants),
+      src/resources/level_01_data.tres (platform positions)
+DELIVERABLE: A table of platform heights vs. leap clearance, showing whether
+the current -630/-570 values clear every platform.
+DO NOT: Change any code. Just verify the math.
+```
+
+### Example: Grok 4.6 reviews anti-stuck design
+
+```
+TASK: Review the anti-stuck progress timer in auditor.gd and claim_jumper.gd
+for regression risks.
+READ: src/boss/auditor.gd (STUCK_TIMEOUT, _stuck_timer, vault logic),
+      src/boss/claim_jumper.gd (same)
+DELIVERABLE: List of edge cases where the vault could fire incorrectly,
+and whether the 3s cooldown is sufficient.
+DO NOT: Rewrite the logic. Just audit it.
+```
+
+### Example: DeepSeek does FSM analysis
+
+```
+TASK: Trace the Claim Jumper's state machine when the boss is at the arena
+east boundary and the player is to the west.
+READ: src/boss/claim_jumper.gd (PATROL state, _ground_chase, _clamp_to_arena,
+      arena-boundary guard)
+DELIVERABLE: Frame-by-frame trace showing velocity.x, is_on_wall(),
+      at_arena_boundary, want_hop for 5 frames.
+DO NOT: Change any code. Just trace the logic.
+```
+
+## Workspace Structure
+
+```
+GM-GAME/
+├── CLAUDE.md                          ← ONE entry point for ALL models
+├── STATUS.md                          ← Living report (what changed, what's next)
+├── .claude/
+│   ├── context-manifests/
+│   │   ├── default.md                 ← Always-load set + on-demand routing
+│   │   ├── shooter.md                 ← v1.2 Blunt Force manifest
+│   │   └── icp.md                     ← Canister layer manifest
+│   └── skills/                        ← Claude Code skills
+├── src/                               ← The actual Godot project
+│   ├── boss/
+│   │   ├── auditor.gd                 ← Boss 1
+│   │   ├── claim_jumper.gd            ← Boss 3
+│   │   └── boss_base.gd               ← Shared base class
+│   ├── level/
+│   │   ├── level_base.gd              ← Shared level logic
+│   │   ├── level_01_smoke_realm.gd    ← Level 1
+│   │   └── level_03_gold_rush.gd      ← Level 3
+│   └── ...
+├── tests/                             ← Verification gates
+└── docs/
+    └── multi-model-guide.md           ← This file
+```
+
+## The Routing Table (from CLAUDE.md)
+
+| Task | Go to | Read | Skills |
+|------|-------|------|--------|
+| Design a level, mechanic, or boss | /design | CONTEXT.md | — |
+| Create art/audio specs or style guide | /assets | CONTEXT.md | pixel-art-skill |
+| Write code, build scenes, configure engine | /src | `.claude/context-manifests/default.md` | gdscript-skill |
+| Write docs, marketing, or changelogs | /docs | CONTEXT.md | — |
+
+## Rules for Multi-Model Work
+
+1. **One CLAUDE.md, never per-model.** The root file routes all models to the
+   right workspace. A model that needs more context gets a focused packet, not
+   a competing CLAUDE.md.
+
+2. **One STATUS.md.** Every model that ships a change updates the same
+   STATUS.md. This is how you know what's actually deployed vs. what's claimed.
+
+3. **One shared model per concept.** Boss AI changes go through the boss
+   files (auditor.gd, claim_jumper.gd, boss_base.gd). Network calls go through
+   Web3Bridge. Level structure goes through level_base.gd. Never patch the same
+   concept in five places.
+
+4. **Context packets, not full repo dumps.** Give each model:
+   - The specific files it needs (2-8k tokens)
+   - The acceptance criteria (what gate proves it works)
+   - The guardrails (what NOT to touch)
+   - The shared model (which autoload/base class owns this change)
+
+5. **Verify before claiming.** A model that says "fixed" without running the
+   verification gates has not fixed anything. The gates are:
+   - `gdparse <changed>.gd` (syntax check)
+   - Godot headless export (real compile)
+   - `node scripts/verify-game.mjs <url>` (browser test)
+   - `bash scripts/security-sentinel.sh` (security scan)
+
+## Per-Model Strengths (from the Grok residual)
+
+| Model | Best at | Context packet |
+|-------|---------|----------------|
+| Kimi K3 | Exact arithmetic, jump math, geometry | Give it the constants + level data, ask for a math table |
+| Grok 4.6 | Anti-stuck design risks, rejection criteria | Give it the fix, ask for edge cases and regressions |
+| Qwen3 | Vision analysis of screenshots | Give it the screenshot, ask what the boss is stuck on |
+| DeepSeek v4 | FSM tracing, state-machine logic | Give it the state machine, ask for a frame-by-frame trace |
+| Codex | Independent code audit | Give it the diff, ask for issues |
+| Claude/Fable | Integration, shipping, Playwright | Give it all packets, ask it to integrate and ship |
